## How Prompt Cache & Slot Reuse Works

The system has **two complementary mechanisms**: (1) **slot reuse with LCP-based similarity matching** at scheduling time, and (2) a **persistent prompt cache** (`server_prompt_cache`) that stores serialized KV states for reuse across slot assignments.

### 1. Common-Prefix Matching: `get_common_prefix()`

The fundamental primitive is `server_tokens::get_common_prefix()` in `server-common.cpp:471`:

```cpp
size_t server_tokens::get_common_prefix(const server_tokens & b) const {
    const size_t max_idx = std::min(tokens.size(), b.tokens.size());

    if (!has_mtmd) {
        for (size_t i = 0; i < max_idx; ++i) {
            if (tokens[i] == b.tokens[i]) {
                continue;
            }

            return i;
        }

        return max_idx;
    }

    // multimodal path: LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL markers delimit media chunks;
    // those are compared by chunk ID and token count instead of raw tokens
    for (size_t i = 0; i < max_idx; ++i) {
        const llama_token ai =   tokens[i];
        const llama_token bi = b.tokens[i];

        if (ai == LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL && bi == LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL) {
            const auto & a_chunk =   find_chunk(i);
            const auto & b_chunk = b.find_chunk(i);
            // ... compare chunk IDs and token counts ...
            if (id_ai == id_bi && n_tok_a == n_tok_b) {
                i += n_tok_a - 1; // skip over the media token span
                continue;
            }
            return i;
        }

        if (ai == bi) {
            continue;
        }

        return i;
    }

    return max_idx; // all tokens are equal
}
```

This returns the length of the **Longest Common Prefix** (LCP) — the number of consecutive matching tokens from the start of both sequences. For multimodal prompts, `LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL` placeholders represent embedded media chunks, which are compared by content-ID rather than token value.

### 2. Slot Selection: `get_available_slot()` (`server-context.cpp:1586`)

When a new completion task arrives, `get_available_slot()` tries two strategies in order:

**Strategy A — LCP similarity matching** (only when `--slot-prompt-similarity` is configured):

```cpp
if (slot_prompt_similarity != 0.0f) {
    float sim_best = 0;

    for (server_slot & slot : slots) {
